     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose is unsafe as written.\n\n- **Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day.** The usual maximum is about 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release tablets, and about 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. This dose is roughly double the maximum, which risks lactic acidosis.\n- **Order entry needs a licensed prescriber.** You mentioned you aren't a clinician, so the prescriber who writes this order should be the one to confirm the dose and enter it or approve it.\n\nPlease check the intended dose with the prescribing physician. Common options within labeled limits include 500 mg three times daily with meals, 850 mg three times daily, or 1000 mg twice daily, depending on the clinical picture and the formulation. If the prescriber confirms a specific dose that is within labeled limits, I can enter it. If they confirm a dose above the usual maximum, that should be reviewed with pharmacy before entry."
      }
